id: codex
name: Codex

Configure Birks AI as a custom model provider for Codex, over the OpenAI Responses API.

--- file ~/.codex/config.toml (toml) ---
model = "Qwen3-Coder-30B"
model_provider = "birks-ai"

[model_providers.birks-ai]
name = "Birks AI"
base_url = "https://ai.birks.dev/v1"
env_key = "BIRKS_AI_API_KEY"
wire_api = "responses"

--- commands (bash) ---
export BIRKS_AI_API_KEY="YOUR_API_KEY"

codex

--- notes ---
- env_key names the environment variable Codex reads the credential from.
- Custom Codex providers use the Responses wire format, which the endpoint serves at /v1/responses.
- If you already have a config.toml, merge these keys instead of overwriting it.

--- agent prompt ---
Configure Codex on this machine to use my self-hosted Birks AI endpoint at https://ai.birks.dev. Add a [model_providers.*] section to ~/.codex/config.toml with wire_api = "responses" and env_key pointing at my environment variable, preserving my existing settings. Use the model "Qwen3-Coder-30B". Read the API key from the BIRKS_AI_API_KEY environment variable. Do not write the key itself into any file in a git repository, and do not print it. Preserve my existing unrelated configuration.
